(No agronomist has checked this plan. It is built from your own map, from climate and soil data measured by satellites and global) Tj
T* (models, and from published South African growing guidelines. It is put together carefully and in good faith - but it is a starting point,) Tj
T* (not an instruction.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
11.5 TL
0.125 0.098 0.059 rg
54. 249.7899999999999636 Td
(Use your own judgement alongside it. A computer cannot see your land. It does not know where the water stands after heavy rain,) Tj
T* (which corner the frost settles in, what failed here last year, or what your family will actually eat. You do.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
11.5 TL
0.125 0.098 0.059 rg
54. 223.7899999999999636 Td
(Soil is the figure most likely to be wrong. Ours comes from a global model that reads a wide area, and real soil can change from) Tj
T* (one end of a single field to the other. If any number here matters to a decision you are spending money on, a soil test is the only) Tj
T* (way to know. You can upload one and the plan will be rebuilt around your real numbers.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
11.5 TL
0.125 0.098 0.059 rg
54. 186.2899999999999636 Td
(Show this to your local agricultural extension officer. They know your district, your rainfall and your pests in a way no model does,) Tj
T* (and they can correct in ten minutes what would otherwise cost you a season. It costs nothing, and it is the single most useful thing) Tj
T* (you can do with this document.) Tj
ET
